# Angular web build check

After any change under `web/` (components, templates, styles, i18n, routes, services, models), run a production build before considering the work complete:

```bash
cd web && yarn ng build
```

Use **Yarn** only (`yarn ng build`), not npm.

## Fix before done

- Treat compile errors, template errors (e.g. pipes in event bindings), and unused-import warnings that fail the build as blockers.
- Fix them in the same session; do not leave a broken `ng build`.
- Prefer `yarn ng build` over relying only on `yarn test:ci` / `yarn lint` — the production build catches template binding and bundling issues those may miss.

